  "findings": {
    "first_sit_fall": "At18:55:38.979, after about203s of active Sit controller, sit_idle frame194 queued0. Operator reported spontaneous tilt/fall. No nonzero cmd_vel appears before this event in the voice recording; manual arrows occurred later.",
    "failed_recoveries": "Walking controller activations at8233.593 and8243.609 were followed by tilt-stops at8236.652 and8246.691, about3.1s later; these are separate from the later manual-arrow fall.",
    "manual_sequence": "59 velocity-command completions plus 1 cancelled velocity job. Explicit backward/forward and both yaw signs appear in timestamped execution logs and ROS cmd_vel. Some adjacent 0.5 s jobs become continuous same-velocity segments. Manual queue accumulation is a concrete software issue, not a demonstrated cause of earlier Sit/final idle falls.",
    "final_idle_fall": "At19:01:55.040,187.27s after last nonzero recorded cmd_vel ended. Published tilt rose4.57\u00b0 at\u22120.5s to28.37\u00b0 at\u22120.1s and59.28\u00b0 atstop, with a large gyro transient. No nonzero command in the preceding 60 s. Operator reported another idle fall.",
    "sensor_consistency": "Large disagreement between quaternion-derived roll/pitch changes and integrated body gyro is present during Sit; earlier nearly level yaw agreement does not generalize to all axes/periods. This identifies inconsistent sensor channels or their interpretation, not a causal parser/actuator diagnosis.",
    "cadence": "One common 575\u2013593 ms publication gap at1793588474.56\u20138475.13 occurs about 40 s beforefinalfall. In the final 10 s before the fall, the maximum IMU receive gap was 9.50 ms. ROS publication/header clocks do not prove physical sensor freshness.",
    "shutdown": "Native manager/hardware deactivation and process exits recorded. API cleanup handler raised RCLError publishingafter rclpy context became invalid; therefore API shutdown was not error-free. This shutdown exception follows all five falls and does not explain them.",
    "connection_loss_stop_audit": "Follow-up audit found no preceding Stop before first Sit tilt; Sit deactivated94.4s afterward. The later voice-close-aligned zero burst occurred while walking remained active,53.7s before final tilt; no controller deactivation until shutdown. This does not identify the fall cause. Separate software-only reproduction: completed idle policy hold survives Stop, while the same hold with a running wait is deactivated."
  },
